From e74c78c3cf25e6579e110be35e2436e105216090 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:17:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(picker): resolve the Codex login and provider-profile
 ids once per model.options pass [daveey]

Why: hub P1 (serve 1757203, c45c7f92) puts model.options at ~105-120 ms/call, .37% of the
rpc/ row (.51% on the run17 heavy serve). Stage timing on the hub (thread CPU, real home):
_apply_capabilities 36 ms; inside it daybreak_offered re-resolved the stored Codex login
(19 x 0.6 ms = 11 ms) and get_model_capabilities/models_dev_id_for re-listed provider profiles
(~430 list_providers() per pass).

What: agent/pass_memo.PassMemo, a ContextVar memo that lives for one pass only (closed on exit,
so copy_context() workers cannot read or fill it afterwards; exceptions release it).
build_models_payload opens it for the models.dev profile-id map; _apply_capabilities opens it
for the stored-login token. Nothing survives the pass: a login/refresh/disable, registry
change, plugin install or home switch is visible on the next call. Explicit tokens bypass it.
A registry-keyed cross-pass memo was built first and rejected in design review: registry
restores that bypass register_provider and the generation-before-publish window can serve
stale answers.

Proof: tests/agent/test_picker_pass_costs.py 15 tests, 11 RED on the base (5 stored-login
reads vs 1). 127 consumer files, 2111 passed. Hub A/B, 4 alternating fresh processes, thread
CPU: base min 81.5 / p50 83-92 ms -> new min 65.5 / p50 66-69 ms. model.options payload is
byte-identical (sort_keys JSON diff of back-to-back base vs new dumps = 0 lines).
